                <pb facs="0106" n="12" sameAs="frus:frus1887/pg12"/>

                <head>No. 11.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Quesada to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Argentine Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-04-11"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 11, 1887</date>.
                        (Received April 12.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inform your excellency
                    that I have received instructions from the minister of foreign affairs to
                    communicate to your excellency, begging you to be so good as to lay it before
                    the President, the great satisfaction with which was received the notice of your
                    legation in the Argentine Republic being raised to the rank of a first-class
                    mission 5 since my Government sees in it a proof of sympathy between the two
                    nations, as well as a desire to strengthen the relations which unite them on the
                    basis of reciprocity.</p>
                <p>In carrying out these instructions I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Vicente G.
                    Quesada.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
